WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.720
- I'm Ben. It's very nice to meet you.

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:02.850
You have a lovely daughter.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.405
I hope you like the tattoo.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.250
- What!

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.083
- Oh, shit.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:08.989
Oh, no.

00:00:08.989 --> 00:00:12.822
(rhythmic instrumental music)

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.980
Fuck it is probably something you'd see

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.670
tattooed on someone's inner-lip.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.600
Perhaps no other tattoo is
as easily hidden as this one.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.990
So what type of person
gets an inner-lip tattoo

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.130
and why do they get it?

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.880
- I got my lip tattooed
the day after I turned 18.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.310
- I'm obsessed with the Beatles.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.988
I thought I was clever when I was 17.

00:00:34.988 --> 00:00:36.070
- I was kind of spontaneous.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.840
Just kind of my attitude
at the time I think.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:38.950
Like, fuck it, you know?

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.690
- To me, the under-the-lip tattoo

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.330
is just a test run for future tattoos.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.163
- They're just funny.

00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:45.410
- If you wanna get a tattoo

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.830
but you don't want anyone
to see it, get a lip tattoo.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:48.663
- Hi, Buzzfeed.

00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:50.210
My name is Kasie, I'm 20 years old,

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.080
and I've been really wanting
an inner-lip tattoo lately.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.970
- This is Kasie, a college
student and tattoo virgin.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.420
She really wants an inner-lip tattoo

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.180
because she can hide it from her mom.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.013
Yikes.

00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:01.520
And I'm gonna join her
every step of the way.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.353
Oh my god.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.310
And this is Zoey Taylor,

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.940
owner of The Warren Tattoo
Shop in West Hollywood.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.970
She's an incredible tattoo
artist and all around badass.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.630
When I think inner-lip tattoo,

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:16.870
I think joke, I think fuck you
or fuck me or fuck my mouth.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.530
It's always like, really raunchy.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.580
- I think people feel a
little more free to be ballsy

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.120
when they're doing something in that area

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.700
rather than almost any other area.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.700
- The lip is one of the most
hidden locations on the body,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.880
if not the most.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.350
I guess it would only
be you and your dentist

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.200
who really sees this thing.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.060
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.090
It's never gonna be like,
oh shit, it just showed.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.470
- According to the book Inked,

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.160
tattooing the inner-lip
originated in Western culture

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.770
and these tattoos are
usually jokes or expletives.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:47.280
However, other oral tattoos
have a longer history.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.590
People in Hawaii and India

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.690
have been tattooing their
tongues for centuries.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.050
Even today, these tattoos

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.620
are part of the cultural zeitgeist.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.540
The film Black Panther inspired super fans

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.120
to go out and get their own.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.620
As for the tattoo process...

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.830
- It's a mucus membrane

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.060
so there's mucus coming
out through the stencil

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.710
while I'm trying to do it so
you have to be really quick

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.110
and it's really, really
bloody skin so it's just,

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.940
it doesn't behave like any
other place you would tattoo.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.760
- So do you get submissions
and you're like,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.960
"No thanks, it's not really my thing."

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.260
- They're kind of a pain in the butt

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.310
and if I don't have to
deal with them, I don't.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.220
- Are you willing to
make an exception today

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.710
and give someone a lip tattoo?

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:22.940
- Yes. Fuck it.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:23.773
- Fuck it.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.810
Today, Kasie's getting her first tattoo

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.610
and it happens to be on her inner-lip

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.100
so I'm headin' over to the
Kappa Delta House at UCLA

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.360
to find out what it is.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.330
Hey.
- Hello. Hi.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.983
- How are you?
- I'm so good.

00:02:34.983 --> 00:02:36.120
- Hi, how are you doing?

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:36.964
- It's a nice place you got here.

00:02:36.964 --> 00:02:38.052
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:38.052 --> 00:02:39.093
- Is it yours?

00:02:39.093 --> 00:02:40.950
- No, I live in my sorority.
- I know, I'm just kidding.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.860
- Yeah, we can head on inside now.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.830
- Let's go.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.352
Kasie showed me around the sorority house.

00:02:45.352 --> 00:02:47.870
- This is kind of the
main living room area.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.169
- I tried every impress
everyone by playing the piano.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:53.210
(playing "Mad World" on the piano)

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.270
Then she introduced me

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.150
to one of her sisters and friends, Erica.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.860
This is out of character
for her to want a tattoo?

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.693
- One, it's really cool,

00:02:58.693 --> 00:03:01.510
but two, it's so funny
and also totally random.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.040
Kasie's also a total sweetheart,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.960
wants to go to nursing school.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.100
Definitely not something
you would imagine.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:07.933
What are you getting?

00:03:07.933 --> 00:03:09.940
- Originally I wanted to get kayata,

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.860
which, I searched online,
means fuck it in Tagalog,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.180
but I've been leaning maybe
more towards laban lang,

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.590
which means essentially
it's an expression like,

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.570
to be brave, be strong, to fight on.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.640
Whoo! Yeah.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:25.473
- Fight on?

00:03:25.473 --> 00:03:27.260
That's USC's phrase.
- No, no!

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.530
- I mean, I feel like the video's

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:29.765
gonna make this a lot worse.

00:03:29.765 --> 00:03:30.670
You could just get a tattoo

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.700
and your parents would
never find out but now...

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.690
(frightened music)

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.770
- Yeah, I just...

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:39.030
A lot of things happening right now.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.830
- Kasie definitely seemed a little anxious

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.900
about the prospect of
her parents finding out

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.470
so I asked her a little more about it.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:48.020
What do you want this
tattoo to mean to you?

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.720
- I don't know, I think I do risky things

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.350
when I feel things are kind of unstable.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.703
This past summer's been the hardest summer

00:03:54.703 --> 00:03:56.100
I've had to deal with yet.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.600
My grandfather got really
sick and fell into a coma.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.850
My mom ended up buying a
last minute plane ticket

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.660
to the Philippines and a
couple hours later he passed.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.420
Everything just started
clashing and closing in on me.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.780
It's really easy to be in a
big school across the country,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.130
to feel really small.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.730
It would just kind of connect
me in someway back home.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.900
- Does anyone in your family have tattoos?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.060
- No.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.570
- You're the first?
- I'm the first.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.403
- Wow.

00:04:23.403 --> 00:04:25.920
What do you imagine your
mom's reaction would be?

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.160
- My mom doesn't even like makeup.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.810
She doesn't like anything on my face

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.460
so having a tattoo on my face...

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.470
- Well, it's like, under your face.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.930
- No, no, she would hate it.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.170
- Kasie's mom, please don't hate me.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.960
I'm so sorry,

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.958
but it's time for her to
spread her wings and fly.

00:04:41.958 --> 00:04:45.040
(laughter)

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:45.873
We hopped in the car

00:04:45.873 --> 00:04:47.640
and hit the road back over to The Warren,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.479
but first, a little rave music.

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:51.896
(rave music)

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.800
- Do you know anything
about how long they last?

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:57.960
- In my experience,

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.292
they don't seem like a
gradually fading thing.

00:05:00.292 --> 00:05:01.740
- I mean, I was under the impression

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.460
that they disappeared after five years.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.230
- I've not found that to be true.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:10.050
- You known it be that
they last permanently?

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.860
- I've known people for 15 years

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.910
who still have the same lookin' lip tattoo

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.260
and it hasn't changed.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.650
- Does that change your way
of thinking about this at all?

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.720
- We're you hoping it was temporary?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.080
- It still hasn't really hit me yet

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.520
that this is gonna happen.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.040
Do you want this to stay

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.810
or do you want it to
disappear after five years?

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:29.910
- She like, "I'm out."

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.320
- It's totally up to you.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.190
- I'm okay with that.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.410
- All right, we're all good?

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.070
- Yeah.
- Submit.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.270
- Submit, wow.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.550
- L-A-B-A-N,

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.690
and then a space,

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.709
and then L-A-N-G.

00:05:46.709 --> 00:05:49.710
(relaxed instrumental music)

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.520
- Hold it while I get the edges.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.270
(relaxed instrumental music)

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.400
- There's no turning
back after this point.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.233
You sure?

00:06:01.926 --> 00:06:03.936
(tattoo machine buzzing)

00:06:03.936 --> 00:06:07.686
(relaxed instrumental music)

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.680
10 being the most painful,
how painful is it right now?

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.808
Seven? Six or seven.

00:06:17.808 --> 00:06:21.558
(relaxed instrumental music)

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.257
Are we done?
- Yeah.

00:06:33.332 --> 00:06:34.830
- You ready to see your first ink?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.340
- Yeah, I wanna see it.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.280
- Go ahead.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.680
- Oh my gosh, you're kidding me.

00:06:45.276 --> 00:06:46.109
So cool.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.580
Yeah, this is exactly what I wanted.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.670
- It was awesome seeing
how pumped Kasie was

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.900
about her first ink.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.600
She loved it so much actually

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.210
that she did something
none of us expected.

00:06:59.369 --> 00:07:00.790
Oh, yeah.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.640
No, I love it.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.360
I don't care what she
thinks at this point.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.560
- You don't?
- Maybe later.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.210
But I'm just on a rush right now.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:14.870
Momma.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:15.710
- What's up? What's up, hun?

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.040
- What's up, boy?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.910
What are you doing, Momma?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.800
- Oh, not much.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.390
- Yeah, I've just been studying all day,

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:25.191
but I wanna show you something.

00:07:25.191 --> 00:07:26.760
- Okay.
- Okay, ready?

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:29.000
- Look.

00:07:31.371 --> 00:07:32.204
- Ew.

00:07:32.204 --> 00:07:33.037
- Ew?

00:07:33.991 --> 00:07:35.893
- It say's laban lang.

00:07:35.893 --> 00:07:36.895
- Laban lang?

00:07:36.895 --> 00:07:38.280
That's a lot of words.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.830
- Yeah, that's two words, Momma.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:41.663
It's hidden.

00:07:41.663 --> 00:07:43.240
Only me and you can see it, Momma.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.810
- Momma, no, I don't laugh like that.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:49.643
- Hello.

00:07:49.643 --> 00:07:51.710
I'm partly responsible for this.

00:07:54.498 --> 00:07:56.300
Oh, shit.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.260
Oh, no.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.410
- This is the artist, Momma.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:00.243
- Hello.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.420
- It's cursive.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.990
It's well done.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.150
- Aw, Mommy.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.220
I wanna hug you.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.180
Okay, so now I can get more, yeah?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.710
- I love you very, very much.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.570
- Bye.

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.403
Yes!

00:08:20.403 --> 00:08:21.390
- She is so sweet.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.610
- I'm so blown away about how she reacted.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.680
- Me too.
- Yeah.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.790
- At the end of the day,

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.520
I think my mom always trusts
my judgment on things.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.760
- Whether it's a first foray into tattoos,

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.820
a spontaneous moment with
friends or something deeper,

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.050
at the end of the day, like all tattoos,

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.620
it is what you make it.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.294
In other words, fuck it.

00:08:43.294 --> 00:08:46.794
(upbeat electronic music)

